1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,070
You have just been born. Welcome.

2
00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:07,020
Before you even take a proper breath,
I need to tell you something.

3
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:09,040
You have also just been hired.

4
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:12,580
No interview. No contract. No salary.

5
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,600
And no resignation letter.

6
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,470
Because this job does not have one.

7
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:19,410
You are the firstborn.

8
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:22,680
And in an African family,
that is not a position.

9
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,310
It is a career.

10
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:27,440
So let’s walk through your entire life.

11
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,130
Stay with me, because by the end,

12
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:32,680
somebody in your family might be
about to call you for something.

13
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:35,630
Right now, your parents have no idea
what they are doing.

14
00:00:35,630 --> 00:00:38,680
Zero. But they are very serious about it.

15
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,630
You sneeze once, and it is an emergency.

16
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:45,490
They carry you to the hospital
with a bag like they are relocating.

17
00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:48,930
Three years later, your little brother
sneezes the same sneeze.

18
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:50,140
“Give him water.”

19
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:53,040
You are version 1.0, full of bugs,

20
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:56,870
and your parents are fixing you,
live, in production.

21
00:00:56,870 --> 00:00:59,550
And the rules. Oh, the rules.

22
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:03,430
No sweets, no biscuits before dinner,
bed at seven.

23
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:06,840
Your younger sibling will be eating
biscuits at midnight in front of the TV

24
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,750
and nobody will say a word.

25
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:11,940
You were the experiment.
They were the scientists.

26
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,800
Your siblings get the stable release.

27
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,580
Then a baby arrives.

28
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:19,120
And your mother looks at you.
You know the look.

29
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,800
You are six years old
and you have just been promoted.

30
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:26,620
“Carry your sister. Watch your brother.
Don’t let him touch that.”

31
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:30,290
You are six.
You can barely carry your own school bag.

32
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:32,990
Now, here is the rule of the house.
It is very simple.

33
00:01:32,990 --> 00:01:35,740
If the small one cries, you did it.

34
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:37,810
You say, “I didn’t even touch him.”

35
00:01:37,810 --> 00:01:39,960
They say, “Then why is he crying?”

36
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,780
That is it. That is the whole case.

37
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:44,470
No evidence. Judgment already passed.

38
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:47,480
And when you are really in trouble,
listen for it.

39
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:50,320
“First name. Middle name. Surname.”

40
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:53,540
By the time they reach the surname,
you are already apologising

41
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:55,900
and you still do not know the crime.

42
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,680
“Go and buy salt.” You go. You come back.

43
00:01:58,680 --> 00:01:59,960
“Where is the change?”

44
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:04,770
You give it, all of it, to the last kobo,
because this family audits.

45
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:07,640
And when your younger one misbehaves,

46
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,020
“Look at your big brother.
Did he do this?”

47
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:13,170
You are standing right there.
You are now a poster.

48
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:16,960
A moving, breathing,
water-carrying poster.

49
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:21,050
Now you are a teenager, and your grades
do not belong to you anymore.

50
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:23,000
They belong to the family.

51
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,790
Your parents’ friends know your results
before you do.

52
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:27,560
An auntie calls from another state.

53
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,110
“I heard you came first.”

54
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:32,200
How? You have not even told anyone.

55
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:35,730
And the careers?
You have exactly three choices.

56
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:38,050
Doctor, lawyer, engineer.

57
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:40,250
Four, if the family
is feeling adventurous,

58
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:42,630
and the fourth one is also doctor.

59
00:02:42,630 --> 00:02:45,660
You say,
“I would like to do something creative.”

60
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:46,990
The room goes silent.

61
00:02:46,990 --> 00:02:49,680
Somebody has to go and hold your mother.

62
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:51,890
And of course,
there is the neighbour’s child.

63
00:02:51,890 --> 00:02:53,570
You have never spoken to this child,

64
00:02:53,570 --> 00:02:57,110
but this child is somehow
in your house every single day.

65
00:02:57,110 --> 00:03:00,300
“Mrs. Okafor’s son is already
reading in his sleep.”

66
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:01,620
Good for him.

67
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:03,970
Here is the part nobody says out loud.

68
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:05,860
Your younger siblings are watching.

69
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:10,120
If you succeed, they have a path.
If you fail, they have a warning.

70
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,630
So you cannot fail.

71
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:13,360
You are not studying for yourself.

72
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,540
You are studying for
the whole queue behind you.

73
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:18,660
You graduate. You get a job.

74
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:20,210
First salary alert.

75
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:23,040
You feel like a champion,
you open your banking app,

76
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:25,440
and for exactly four minutes,
you are happy.

77
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:27,780
Then the calls start.

78
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:30,010
“My dear, I don’t want to disturb you.”

79
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:31,500
That is how it always starts.

80
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:34,630
They do not want to disturb you,
then the disturbance arrives.

81
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:39,630
School fees. Rent. A hospital bill.
“Just a small thing.”

82
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:41,490
Some people call it black tax.

83
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:47,140
Whatever you call it, the invoice is real,
and nobody asked if you have a budget.

84
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:50,190
Congratulations,
you are now the family bank.

85
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:54,430
No interest, no collateral,
and no customer care.

86
00:03:54,430 --> 00:03:57,380
You say, “But who is paying my own rent?”

87
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,970
And somebody says, “God will provide.”

88
00:03:59,970 --> 00:04:04,100
And he does.
But somehow, he keeps using your account.

89
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:08,060
And the funny thing is, you do it.
Because you love them.

90
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:11,240
When your younger sister walks
across that graduation stage,

91
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:14,580
the one you paid for,
you will cry harder than she does.

92
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:18,170
Even if you are pretending
it is dust in your eye.

93
00:04:18,170 --> 00:04:20,940
By 30, your job title has changed again.

94
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:23,220
You are now management.

95
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:26,980
At every wedding, every funeral,
every naming ceremony,

96
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:29,440
you are somehow in charge of something.

97
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:33,210
Somebody turns to you and says,
“Who is handling the rice?”

98
00:04:33,210 --> 00:04:36,730
“Why do I know about rice?
I came here to attend.”

99
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:41,090
Uncles who have not spoken in five years
will only talk through you.

100
00:04:41,090 --> 00:04:44,880
Two cousins are fighting,
and you are the United Nations.

101
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:48,680
And then there is the question
that has followed you since you were 25.

102
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:52,170
“So, when are we eating your rice?”

103
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:54,940
Not if. When.

104
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:56,590
Now, let’s be honest for a minute.

105
00:04:56,590 --> 00:04:58,660
All of this is funny, and it is,

106
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:02,900
but if you are a firstborn,
you are also tired.

107
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:05,230
And there is a reason this role exists.

108
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:08,910
It is not that you are the strongest.
It is that you were first.

109
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:12,420
That is all. Position, not talent.

110
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:15,950
Your parents did not test you and decide
you were the most capable.

111
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:18,360
They were scared. They were learning.

112
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:21,150
And you were the one standing closest.

113
00:05:21,150 --> 00:05:23,170
Here is the part worth knowing.

114
00:05:23,170 --> 00:05:25,080
A lot of that pressure is love,

115
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:28,590
said in a language that does not know
how to say it softly.

116
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:31,910
“Be responsible” often means
“we are afraid.”

117
00:05:31,910 --> 00:05:34,880
“Don’t disappoint us” often means
“we are counting on you

118
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:37,530
because we do not know
who else to count on.”

119
00:05:37,530 --> 00:05:42,580
You can understand that and still say,
“This is too heavy.”

120
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:45,350
So here is something
you can do this month.

121
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:47,560
Pick one thing you carry.

122
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:52,650
One bill, one phone call,
one decision that always lands on you.

123
00:05:52,650 --> 00:05:54,680
Say it out loud to the family.

124
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:59,300
“This is now shared.”
Not as a fight, as a plan.

125
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:01,850
Give it a name and give it a person.

126
00:06:01,850 --> 00:06:05,920
You would be surprised how many people
were waiting to be asked.

127
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:08,420
So that is your whole life.

128
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:12,920
Born, hired, promoted, never paid.

129
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:15,870
If you are a firstborn,
tell me in the comments.

130
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:19,590
What is the most responsible thing
you have ever been asked to do?

131
00:06:19,590 --> 00:06:22,500
I want to see who has been
carrying the whole house.

132
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:25,720
And if you are the baby of the family
laughing right now and thinking,

133
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:28,010
“I don’t know what she is talking about,”

134
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:30,920
I know. That is the problem.

135
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,720
Call your elder sibling today.

136
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,070
Don’t ask for anything.

137
00:06:34,070 --> 00:06:36,240
Just say, “How are you?”

138
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,870
And watch what happens.

139
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:40,240
They might not even know what to say.

140
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,860
See you in the next one.

